      "summary": "Calls other than modeled .update() and other unsupported mutations can be skipped while stale schema is retained. m.clear()/pop()/helper mutation can remove a key at runtime that the analyzer still approves."
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "title": "workflow manifest binding and key-access tracing is partial",
      "evidence_lines": [
        "scripts/arc_workflow_preflight.py:359-378",
        "scripts/arc_workflow_preflight.py:381-409",
        "docs/workflow-preflight.md:19-20",
        "tests/test_arc_workflow_preflight.py:164-184"
      ],
      "summary": "json.loads is treated as tied to the manifest when its argument merely mentions the path variable, and only bracket key chains are extracted. A valid bracket read can mask an unsupported d.get('ghost') read, allowing a false PASS."
